is gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({x}^{2}+\\frac{5}{4}) & =0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+5 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308983 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308984 13194139534769 true] [17592186308983 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308985 13194139534769 true] [17592186308983 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308986 13194139534769 true] [17592186308983 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308987 13194139534769 true] [17592186308983 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308988 13194139534769 true] [17592186308983 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534769 true] [17592186308983 1041 "selection" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308983 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308988 13194139534769 true] [17592186308983 1110 #uuid "e5749261-77b3-5477-939e-e5a283bd4e18" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308984 1034 "4{x}^{2}-2=0" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308984 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534769 true] [17592186308984 1111 #uuid "da29b910-b7de-507f-9279-daa655082755" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308985 1034 "4{x}^{2}+3=0" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308985 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534769 true] [17592186308985 1111 #uuid "56e88c15-91d7-565b-82f3-bf726ee486b7" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308986 1034 "4{x}^{2}+2=0" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308986 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534769 true] [17592186308986 1111 #uuid "88aca4c2-1d2f-5228-a2da-cffb31a74262" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308987 1034 "4{x}^{2}-3=0" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308987 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534769 true] [17592186308987 1111 #uuid "2d2502c8-c042-513b-bbc6-0880c2ac691e" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308988 1034 "4{x}^{2}+5=0" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308988 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534769 true] [17592186308988 1111 #uuid "3de3fdcb-71f5-5254-9433-21250163d792" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308989 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308990 13194139534769 true] [17592186308989 1089 "q-160008" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308989 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534769 true] [17592186308989 1100 "A quadratic equation in the variable $x$ with real coefficients has a root $x=2+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}.$ Given that the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ in the equation is $2$, find the equation." 13194139534769 true] [17592186308989 1113 #uuid "2095c4b9-c0bc-5ea3-a485-0afbc68ba43f" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308989 1145 "Since the quadratic equation has real coefficients and $x=2+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}$ is a root, its conjugate $x=2-\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}$ must also be a root. Therefore, using the zero product property, we can write a quadratic equation with the required roots as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-(2+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}))(x-(2-\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}))=0\n$$\n\nBy expanding the parentheses, we can write the equation in standard form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-x(2-\\sqrt{3}\\text{i})-x(2+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i})+(2+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i})(2-\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+\\sqrt{3}x\\text{i}-2x-\\sqrt{3}x\\text{i}+4-(\\sqrt{3}\\text{i})^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+4+3 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+7 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation has roots $x=2\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i},$ but the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ is not $2.$ Therefore, to find the desired equation, we multiply the equation above by $2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}^{2}-4x+7) & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-8x+14 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308991 13194139534769 true] [17592186308990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308992 13194139534769 true] [17592186308990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308993 13194139534769 true] [17592186308990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308994 13194139534769 true] [17592186308990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308995 13194139534769 true] [17592186308990 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534769 true] [17592186308990 1041 "selection" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308990 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308995 13194139534769 true] [17592186308990 1110 #uuid "22048be0-e859-5cfc-9c60-8936d0726416" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308991 1034 "2{x}^{2}-16x-14=0" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308991 1103 #edb/re