 =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4(-1) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+4 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation has roots $x=\\pm 2\\text{i},$ but the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ is not $10.$ Therefore, to find the desired equation, we multiply the equation above by $10.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10({x}^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ 10{x}^{2}+40 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308997 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308998 13194139534769 true] [17592186308997 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534769 true] [17592186308997 1041 "field-1" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308997 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308998 13194139534769 true] [17592186308997 1110 #uuid "48b8c144-ca6d-5fa6-92b8-3831c408f8c7" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308998 1034 "10x^2+40" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308998 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534769 true] [17592186308998 1111 #uuid "6a801935-d0fa-585b-ac1c-fdb44d39443e" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308999 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309000 13194139534769 true] [17592186308999 1089 "q-28219" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308999 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534769 true] [17592186308999 1100 "A quadratic equation in the variable $x$ with real coefficients has a root $x=2-\\text{i}.$ Given that the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ in the equation is $2$, find the equation." 13194139534769 true] [17592186308999 1113 #uuid "2a38a23c-d1f3-5a91-bfc6-a693e8120f55" 13194139534769 true] [17592186308999 1145 "Since the quadratic equation has real coefficients and $x=2-\\text{i}$ is a root, its conjugate $x=2+\\text{i}$ must also be a root. Therefore, using the zero product property, we can write a quadratic equation with the required roots as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-(2-\\text{i}))(x-(2+\\text{i}))=0\n$$\n\nBy expanding the parentheses, we can write the equation in standard form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-x(2+\\text{i})-x(2-\\text{i})+(2-\\text{i})(2+\\text{i}) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x-x\\text{i}-2x+x\\text{i}+4-{\\text{i}}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+4+1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation has roots $x=2\\pm \\text{i},$ but the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ is not $2.$ Therefore, to find the desired equation, we multiply the equation above by $2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}^{2}-4x+5) & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-8x+10 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534769 true] [17592186309000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309001 13194139534769 true] [17592186309000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309002 13194139534769 true] [17592186309000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309003 13194139534769 true] [17592186309000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309004 13194139534769 true] [17592186309000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309005 13194139534769 true] [17592186309000 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534769 true] [17592186309000 1041 "selection" 13194139534769 true] [17592186309000 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309003 13194139534769 true] [17592186309000 1110 #uuid "38a8962b-84c2-562f-8c12-f4d5e6437e3f" 13194139534769 true] [17592186309001 1034 "2{x}^{2}-8x+5=0" 13194139534769 true] [17592186309001 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534769 true] [17592186309001 1111 #uuid "8356454d-b49f-5d62-915d-46613aad928f" 13194139534769 true] [17592186309002 1034 "2{x}^{2}+8x-10=0" 13194139534769 true] [17592186309002 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534769 true] [17592186309002 1111 #uuid "7ded88d4-ed79-54df-8d41-c83aaad2920c" 13194139534769 true] [17592186309003 1034 "2{x}^{2}-8x+10=0" 13194139534769 true] [17592186309003 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534769 true] [17592186309003 1111 #uuid "490f7140-c7b2-5e77-a27c-258005a9a15a" 13194139534769 true] [17592186309004 1034 "2{x}^{2}-2x+10=0" 13194139534769 true] [17592186309004 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534769 true] [17592186309004 1111 #uuid "3c828eb2-2017-5275-a9f7-30d008823640" 13194139534769 true] [17592186309005 1034 "2{x}^{2}-4x+5=0" 13194139534769 true] [17592186309005 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534769 true] [17592186309005 1111 #uuid "06ca2dcd-2198-5012-838d-5ff7c23936a3" 13194139534769 true] [17592186309006